INT. FRONTIER SALOON - NIGHT

Piano stops. Chairs scrape. Six figures face off across spilled whiskey.

SHERIFF BOONE (50s) draws. RED CALLOWAY (30s) draws. A bartender, MOSES FULLER (60s), ducks. A schoolteacher, MISS ELOISE TRASK (30s), screams. A drunk, LEFTY OBREGON (40s), laughs. A boy piano player, SILAS CROFT (12), freezes with one finger on a key.

BOONE
Drop it, Red.

^RED
You drop yours.

MOSES
Not in my bar!

ELOISE
Please!

LEFTY
(laughing)
Do it!

Silas presses the key. A single note rings out. All six flinch. Nobody fires.

FADE OUT.
